course: dictionary
lesson: 2373
title: Cloud words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cloud names tell you what a cloud looks like and how high it is. The clue is often in the name itself. «Cumulus are white puffy heaps of fair weather.» The word heap is the clue: cumulus clouds look like piles of cotton wool.
explain: «Cumulus clouds are white and puffy and usually mean fair weather.» The word usually tells you this is the normal sign, not a rule. Fair weather means dry and pleasant, so a cumulus sky is usually a nice one.
explain: Compare the cloud names in a sentence. «Stratus are flat grey sheets that may bring drizzle; cirrus are thin wisps of ice high up.» Cumulus is puffy, stratus is flat, and cirrus is wispy. When you know one name, the others are easier to sort out.
fact: Cumulus is a noun for a type of white, puffy cloud with a flat bottom and a rounded top.
fact: Cumulus clouds form when warm air rises.
fact: Cumulus clouds usually mean fine weather.
fact: A very tall cumulus can grow into a cumulonimbus, a towering storm cloud.
fact: The word cumulus comes from Latin and means "heap".
exercise: «Cumulus clouds are white and puffy and usually mean fair weather.» What does cumulus mean? | A flat grey sheet that brings drizzle | *A type of white, puffy cloud | A thin wisp of ice high in the sky | A dark storm cloud that brings thunder
exercise: «Stratus are flat grey sheets that may bring drizzle.» Which cloud name is for flat grey sheets? | *Stratus | Cumulonimbus | Cumulus | Cirrus
exercise: Which cloud usually means fair weather? | Stratus | Cumulonimbus | *Cumulus | Cirrus
test: Cumulus clouds form when which kind of air rises? | Cold air | *Warm air | Wet air | Dusty air
test: The word cumulus comes from which language, and what does it mean? | *Latin, meaning "heap" | English, meaning "cloud" | Greek, meaning "sky" | French, meaning "wool"
exam: A very tall cumulus can grow into which storm cloud? | Stratus | Cirrus | Cumulus heap | *Cumulonimbus
